	"findings": [
		"311 developer tools were submitted in 2026-08, against 302 in 2025-08: +3%. Uneed launches changed +51% over the same months.",
		"On 2026-09-27, DevHunt's new submit form started filling itself from a website URL. 3,203 tools were submitted in 2026-10. DevHunt says to read this jump as a change to the form, not to demand, so we compare only months before 2026-09.",
		"Share of submissions tagged AI Agents: 8.7% in 2026-08, against 2.6% a year before; MCP: 7.7% in 2026-08, against 2.3% a year before; AI Coding: 3.2% in 2026-08, against 0.7% a year before. DevHunt added these categories in 2026 and tagged older tools once, so the history is its classifier's reading.",
		"Launch counts follow DevHunt's free queue and pricing more than demand. 2025-01 and 2026-01 hold large batches of queued free tools, so we use submissions.",
		"DevHunt logs 16 changes to its pricing, launch queue, moderation and categories since 2024-03-05. The paywall of 2024-11-05 cut submissions, which shows how much the site's own rules move these counts.",
		"Tools later deleted or blocked are left out of every month, so past months can go down slightly. This is one site for developer tools, and its growth may reflect the site itself."
	],
